ac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343429" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ 2, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\ -4 & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c27f888db73e9218f13f2a0fd95417ea6166039b0f201dbe1e72e822dea2850"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1)^{n+1}"] ["math" "(-1)^{n}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1)^{n}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/que