fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343421" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343421" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343421" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343421" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $F(x)=|x|$ defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}(2n-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1 & =-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c27f888db73e9218f13f2a0fd95417ea6166039b0f201dbe1e72e822dea2850"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1)^{n+1}"] ["math" "(-1)^{n}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "continuous"] ["text" "discontinuous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "continuous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-343395" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ 1, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{1}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\pi (2n-1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )=(-1)^{n+1}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n+1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c27f888db73e9218f13f2a0fd95417ea6166039b0f201dbe1e72e822dea2850"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1)^{n+1}"] ["math" "(-1)^{n}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1)^{n+1}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "continuous"] ["text" "discontinuous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "continuous"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "q-342571" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/state.json" "file_sha256" "8911c50d090842de3ae01755710c0fb34b50ac855d8d5af09e7a6a44a50dd853"} {"question" "e-21865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/assets/73b3d7951ab2c2a355763f71d2dd97dc4c9c5921bc087ae83af3936b0daf5d8a.png)\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/example-21865.json" "file_sha256" "96601284e2337f6ec2113bf542ab834062b048236e90ff1d06112f45d34ffbc4"} {"question" "e-21865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x) = \\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n\\cos\\bigg(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\bigg)+b_n\\sin\\bigg(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\bigg).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x) = f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x) = \\dfrac{f^-(x)+f^+(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $f^-(x)$ and $f^-(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is not continuous at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$ The one-sided limits at this point are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{-}}f(x)=2 \\\\ {f}^{+}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{+}}f(x)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{f^-\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)+f^+\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}{2} = \\dfrac{2+(-1)}{2} = \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{1}{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/example-21865.json" "file_sha256" "96601284e2337f6ec2113bf542ab834062b048236e90ff1d06112f45d34ffbc4"} {"question" "e-21866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/assets/1da7fe97b22b7a72b4253abfb180ce5f294fa945450879d8cb857ee1470edbf3.png)\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)} \\sin((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nUse this Fourier series to find the sum of the series\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/example-21866.json" "file_sha256" "554995a821ddd4d54fbbf6cec2a3bfd0701c666dfc6faaeb3006fa6a8b189f41"} {"question" "e-21866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left((2n-1)\\cdot\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi\\right) = (-1)^{n+1}.\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ into the given Fourier series gives\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)} \\sin\\left((2n-1)\\cdot\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n= \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)}(-1)^{n+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, since $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ the Fourier series converges to $f\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right).$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\in [0,\\pi),$ we have\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{\\pi (2n-1)}(-1)^{n+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{4} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} = \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070509/example-21866.json" "file_sha256" "554995a821ddd4d54fbbf6cec2a3bfd0701c666dfc6faaeb3006fa6a8b189f41"}] "usage" {"e-21865" [] "q-342571" [] "e-21866" []} "basis" 2493 "retractions" [[17592186167232 :question/problem "$F(x) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x ∈ [- π, 0] \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ (0, π)$\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n$f(x)∼\\frac{1}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(2)/(π(2n - 1))\\sin ((2n - 1)x)$.\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x = \\frac{π}{2}$, we have\n$(-1)^{n + 1}$ {{field-1}}"] [17592186166507 :question/problem "${-1,\\begin{vmatrix}x ∈ [- \\frac{π}{2}, 0] \\\\ 2,\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ (0, \\frac{π}{2})$\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$."] [17592186166507 :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x) = \\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n\\cos\\bigg(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\bigg)+b_n\\sin\\bigg(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\bigg)\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x$, then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n$S(x) = f(x)$\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x$, then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n$S(x) = \\dfrac{f^-(x)+f^+(x)}{2}$\nwhere $f^-(x)$ and $f^-(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is not continuous at\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nThe one-sided limits at this point are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{-}(\\frac{π}{2}) &= lim_(x → (π/2)^{-})f(x) = 2 \\\\\nf^{+}(\\frac{π}{2}) &= lim_(x → (π/2)^{+})f(x) =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{f^-\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)+f^+\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}{2} = \\dfrac{2+(-1)}{2} = \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{1}{2}}\n$$"] [17592186166508 :question/problem "${-1,\\begin{vmatrix}x ∈ [- π, 0] \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ (0, π)$\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n$f(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)} \\sin((2n-1)x)$.\nUse this Fourier series to find the sum of the series\n$\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}$."] [17592186166508 :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that at\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left((2n-1)\\cdot\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi\\right) = (-1)^{n+1}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the given Fourier series gives\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)} \\sin\\left((2n-1)\\cdot\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{4}{\\pi(2n-1)}(-1)^{n+1}\n$$\n\nNext, since $f(x)$ is continuous at\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nthe Fourier series converges to\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nSince $[MATH: \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\in [0,\\pi),]$ we have\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(4)/(π(2n - 1))(-1)^{n + 1} \\\\\n\\frac{π}{4} &= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)((-1)^{n + 1})/(2n - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} = \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186164949 17592186164950 17592186164951 17592186164952] "immutable_fields" [[17592186164948 :answer-field/id] [17592186164948 :answer-field/key] [17592186164948 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
